# Who owns what. GitHub reads this to request reviews automatically; a human
# reads it to know who to ask.
#
# HONEST STATE: one person owns everything. This file does not change that — it
# records it, so a stranger can see at a glance that there is no second reviewer
# to fall back on. INVENTORY.md § "What has no backup" prices that risk.
# Adding a second owner here is a real mitigation and costs one line.

*                       @alaap-kwapso

# The law-book and the rules registry travel together — a law without its check
# is forbidden by `registry-integrity`, so these three change as one.
/RULES.md               @alaap-kwapso
/shared/rules/          @alaap-kwapso
/CLAUDE.md              @alaap-kwapso

# The two public doors. Every other worker is private by config; a change here
# can put a new address on the internet.
/workers/gateway/         @alaap-kwapso
/workers/portal-gateway/  @alaap-kwapso

# The agency's own money. Nothing a client login can reach may import this.
/workers/tenancy/src/lib/internal-money.ts  @alaap-kwapso

# Standing the base up, taking a change back out, and what is not in the repo.
/BOOTSTRAP.md           @alaap-kwapso
/RUNBOOK.md             @alaap-kwapso
/INVENTORY.md           @alaap-kwapso
/OPERATIONS.md          @alaap-kwapso

# Real customer data lives behind these — the catalogue is tracked, the data
